:''Not to be confused with the deprecated [[Channeling|Melee Channeling]] (mechanic) or {{M|Energy Channel}} (mod).''

'''Channeled Abilities''' (also known as '''Toggled Abilities''') are [[Warframe]] abilities that consume additional [[Energy]] in some way while active, and can be deactivated manually by recasting. These typically do not have a fixed duration, though this is not always the case.

==Mechanics==
While channeling, most sources of energy restoration (such as {{Focus|Wellspring}} or [[Helminth|Helminth Invigorations]]) are disabled for '''most''' abilities (see ability pages for more details), with the ''only'' exceptions being energy conversion from {{M|Rage}} and {{M|Hunter Adrenaline}}, {{A|Brightbonnet}}, and [[Energy Orb]]. However in rare instances or in the [[Conclave]] game mode, Energy Orbs may be disabled as well.

===Incarnon Genesis===
[[Incarnon Genesis]] perks offer an additional bonus to some weapons while a channeled ability is active, though not all channeled abilities can activate these perks. The abilities which meet Incarnon requirements and allow the use of equipped weapons are:

*{{WF|Baruuk}}'s {{A|Elude}}.
*{{WF|Chroma}}'s {{A|Spectral Scream}} (melee only) or {{A|Effigy}}.
*{{WF|Ember}}'s {{A|Immolation}} when fully heated.
*{{WF|Equinox}}'s {{A|Mend & Maim|Mend}} or {{A|Mend & Maim|Maim}}.
*{{WF|Excalibur}}'s {{A|Exalted Blade}} (Primary and secondary weapons only).
*{{WF|Gara}}'s {{A|Mass Vitrify}} (During expansion only).
*{{WF|Ivara}}'s {{A|Prowl}}.
*{{WF|Mirage}}'s {{A|Prism}}.
*{{WF|Nyx}}'s {{A|Absorb}} with {{M|Assimilate}}.
*{{WF|Oberon}}'s {{A|Renewal}}.
*{{WF|Oraxia}}'s {{A|Silken Stride}} (Primary and secondary weapons only).
*{{WF|Sevagoth}}'s {{A|Gloom}} when draining within enemy range (a [[Helminth]]-transferable ability).
*{{WF|Valkyr}}'s {{A|Hysteria}} (Primary and secondary weapons only).
*{{WF|Wukong}}'s {{A|Primal Fury}} (Primary and secondary weapons only).
The Incarnon Weapons which have such perks include: [[Braton Incarnon Genesis|Braton]], [[Boltor Incarnon Genesis|Boltor]], [[Gorgon Incarnon Genesis|Gorgon]], [[Miter Incarnon Genesis|Miter]], [[Strun Incarnon Genesis|Strun]], [[Gammacor Incarnon Genesis|Gammacor]], [[Kunai Incarnon Genesis|Kunai]], [[Lex Incarnon Genesis|Lex]], [[Magistar Incarnon Genesis|Magistar]], and [[Vectis Incarnon Genesis|Vectis]].

