==How Ability Duration Affects Energy Drain==
[[File:DurationEfficiencyTable.png|right|thumb|300px]]
'''Channeled abilities''' like {{WF|Excalibur}}'s {{A|Exalted Blade}} and {{WF|Oberon}}'s {{A|Renewal}} last for an indefinite amount of time, but drain [[energy]] over time as long as they are active. Channeled abilities remain active until energy is completely depleted or until the ability is manually deactivated (by pressing the ability key again).

The energy drain per second for channeled abilities scales with both {{Stat|Ability Duration}} and {{Stat|Ability Efficiency}}, and follows the formula:

'''<big>M = B * (2 - E) * (1 / D)</big>'''

* '''M''' is the '''modded''' energy drain per second.
* '''B''' is the '''base''' energy drain per second.
* '''E''' is ability '''efficiency''' (in decimal form; uses the ''true value'' before the 175% cap is applied).
* '''D''' is ability '''duration''' (in decimal form).

For example, with 140% duration and 130% efficiency, an ability with a base channeling cost of 10 energy per second will be reduced down to: 10 * (2 - 1.3) * (1 / 1.4) = 5 energy per second. 

'''An important note is that modded channeling cost has a floor of -75% and a ceiling of +75%'''. In other words, a 10 energy/s channeled ability cannot be modded to drain less than 2.5 energy per second, or more than 17.5 energy per second. Because the efficiency stat used in the calculation is '''not''' capped at it's normal maximum of 175%, efficiency values over 175% can be used to negate the increased energy drain from a negative duration stat. A common example of this is using {{M|Fleeting Expertise}} and {{M|Streamline}} together in order to reach the minimum channeling cost, using the 190% efficiency to counteract the penalty of the 40% duration stat.

'''<big>Other Notes:</big>'''

* The chart to the right can be consulted to determine a Warframe ability's modded energy drain per second.<ref>[[User blog:Fegazeus/17.5 Duration mods and drain|User blog - 17.5 Duration & Drain]]</ref>
* '''Energy drain calculation does not snapshot temporary duration or efficiency buffs, and instead updates dynamically'''. Effects such as {{Arcane|Molt Efficiency}} and {{M|Seismic Bond}} therefore do not need to be present when first casting the ability in order for them to affect the drain rate.
**{{WF|Hildryn}}'s own abilities (Haven and Aegis Storm) do snapshot Ability Efficiency and Ability Duration for their drains, while infused abilities through the Helminth system (e.g., {{A|Gloom}}) behave normally.
* It is possible to achieve an efficiency value over 200%, for example using {{M|Boreal's Hatred}}, {{M|Fleeting Expertise}}, and {{M|Streamline}}. Because the formula for modded energy drain uses the non-capped value for efficiency, this will result in the minimum possible energy drain (-75%) regardless of any penalty from negative duration.
* On the other hand, it is easier, and in some case trivial to make up for below 100% efficiency through increased duration (and it's generally better to do it that way than trying to make efficiency positive again). For instance, if you are using {{M|Blind Rage}}:
** Using {{M|Streamline}}, the channeling costs 100% * 125% / 100% = 125% of the base cost.
** Using {{M|Fleeting Expertise}}, the channeling costs 100% * 95% / 40% = 237.5% of the base cost, hitting the ceiling of 175% of the base cost instead.
** Using {{M|Continuity}}, the channeling costs 100% * 155% / 130% = 119.2% of the base cost.
** Using {{M|Narrow Minded}}, the channeling costs 100% * 155% / 199% = 77.9% of the base cost (at the price of ability range).

